’‚¤textÙ2The LORD possessed me in the beginning of his way,¦layout ‚¤text¸Before his works of old.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ2I was set up from everlasting, from the beginning,¦layout ‚¤text¶Or ever the earth was.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ/When there were no depths, I was brought forth;¦layout ‚¤textÙ2When there were no fountains abounding with water.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ"Before the mountains were settled,¦layout ‚¤textÙ%Before the hills was I brought forth:¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ7While as yet he had not made the earth, nor the fields,¦layout ‚¤textÙ.Nor the highest part of the dust of the world.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ*When he prepared the heavens, I was there:¦layout ‚¤textÙ1When he set a compass upon the face of the depth:¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ%When he established the clouds above:¦layout ‚¤textÙ/When he strengthened the fountains of the deep:¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines“‚¤textÙ#When he gave to the sea his decree,¦layout ‚¤textÙ0That the waters should not pass his commandment:¦layout§quote_2‚¤textÙ/When he appointed the foundations of the earth:¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines“‚¤textÙ.Then I was by him, as one brought up with him:¦layout ‚¤text¼And I was daily his delight,¦layout§quote_1‚¤text¼Rejoicing always before him;¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ-Rejoicing in the habitable part of his earth;¦layout ‚¤textÙ*And my delights were with the sons of men.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verse ªlast_verse$¦verses•„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ-Now therefore hearken unto me, O ye children:¦layout ‚¤textÙ'For blessed are they that keep my ways.¦layout§quot